# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""CRGO 0.10.0, second part: security monitoring (SIEM) and security orchestration and response (SOAR)
(specifications of 2026-10-12; decisions S1-S12 in docs/baseline/siem_soar_phase0.md). Same tuple layouts as spec_pca.py.

New modules
  siem   telemetry sources, event records, normalisation profiles and parsers, detection strategies and rules,
         correlation rules, alert disposition, threat indicators and intelligence sources, detection coverage and gaps,
         detection tests, telemetry health, hunting hypotheses, behavioural baselines   (imports incident, grc)
  soar   investigations, incident classification and severity, response playbooks and versions, steps, triggers,
         response actions and their risk class, approval gates and decisions, automation and action executions,
         response evidence, forensic artefacts, incident impact and communications, recovery verification,
         response effectiveness measurements                                            (imports siem, audit)

The boundary of ADR-011 applies: CRGO holds reusable concepts, reference vocabularies and selected records; event
streams, alert instances, execution histories and secrets stay in operational stores, and no inference made in CRGO
ever authorises a production action. An indicator match never implies an incident or an attribution.
"""
